{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7181437","formula":"C₉H₆O₂","hill":"C9H6O2","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":9.0,"H":6.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Phenylpropiolic acid"},"descriptions":{"en":"Phenylpropiolic acid, C6H5CCCO2H, formed by the action of alcoholic potash on cinnamic acid dibromide, C6H5CHBrCHBrCO2H, crystallizes in long needles or prisms which melt at 136–137 °C. When heated with water to 120 °C, it yields phenylacetylene (C6H5CCH). Chromic acid oxidizes it to benzoic acid; zinc and acetic acid reduce it to cinnamic acid, C6H5CH=CHCO2H, whilst sodium amalgam reduces it to hydrocinnamic acid, C6H5CH2CH2CO2H. Ortho-nitrophenylpropiolic acid, NO2C6H4CCCO2H, prepared by the action of alcoholic potash on ortho-nitrocinnamic acid dibromide, crystallizes in needles which decompose when heated to 155–156 °C. It is readily converted into indigo."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":69475,"mass":146.14,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)C#CC(=O)O","inchikey":"XNERWVPQCYSMLC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-phenylprop-2-ynoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"69475","atoms":17,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.809,"y":1.181,"z":-0.098,"el":"O"},{"x":3.868,"y":-1.095,"z":0.091,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.827,"y":-0.009,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.514,"y":1.204,"z":0.045,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.534,"y":-1.211,"z":-0.045,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.909,"y":1.216,"z":0.045,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.929,"y":-1.198,"z":-0.045,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.616,"y":0.015,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.602,"y":-0.022,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":1.805,"y":-0.033,"z":0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":3.245,"y":-0.048,"z":0.004,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.976,"y":2.148,"z":0.081,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.014,"y":-2.164,"z":-0.08,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.443,"y":2.16,"z":0.079,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.481,"y":-2.133,"z":-0.08,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.702,"y":0.024,"z":-0.00